1786289839344836	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzAQ		item.create	bn-28h	{"description":"# Context & Background\nagentbus currently appends normalized events, hook reports, and registrations indefinitely. The verbose event log reached roughly 895 MB after about ten days, and transcript rediscovery can replay old files as new events. The Zellij roster consumes the bounded snapshot, while agentbus wait depends on byte offsets in the unbounded log.\n\n# Goal\nMake all agentbus-owned persistent state bounded while retaining accurate live state, current-or-next completion waits, crash recovery, and nonblocking hooks.\n\n# Approach\nFirst eliminate transcript replay amplification. Then move completion watermarks into a compact bounded projection, rotate the verbose log under byte and age caps, replace append-only hook journals with bounded state/spooling, and verify the deployed service against live agents and Zellij.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Every agentbus-owned data structure has an explicit retention or compaction policy.\n- Transcript inactivity and daemon restarts do not republish historical events as new.\n- wait cannot miss or return a stale completion during resolution, rotation, or restart.\n- Default verbose history is bounded by age and total bytes.\n- Hooks remain quick, lock-free in their hot path, and always exit successfully.\n- Existing UI changes and public query behavior remain intact.\n\n# Project Value\nKeeps agentbus cheap enough to run continuously while preserving its role as the correctness boundary for agent supervision.","kind":"goal","labels":["retention","reliability"],"size":"xl","title":"Bound agentbus storage without weakening wait correctness","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:kRyrHtU7HYihrBmC-uyhHdl_kX-w_43B8qKVzR8Wlwc
1786289880770676	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzAg		item.create	bn-3mg	{"description":"# Context & Background\nMultiTail drops cursors when a transcript ages outside the active window. Rediscovery later tracks that existing file from byte zero, so normalized history is appended again as if it were live. Storage retention cannot work until this amplification stops.\n\n# Goal\nGive every transcript a stable publication cursor and enough parser state to resume after inactivity and daemon restart without replaying old events as news.\n\n# Approach\nSeparate active polling from cursor ownership, persist checkpoints atomically, validate file identity and truncation, and preserve the startup backfill rule that reconstructs snapshots without publishing history.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Aging out and reactivation publishes only bytes appended since the checkpoint.\n- Restart and reactivation do not duplicate already-published history.\n- New, replaced, and truncated transcripts have explicit safe behavior.\n- Cursor files are themselves bounded and stale entries are pruned safely.\n- Tests cover Claude stateful turn reconstruction plus Codex and agy.\n\n# Project Value\nStops the dominant accidental growth source before retention masks it.","kind":"goal","labels":["retention","transcripts"],"parent":"bn-28h","size":"l","title":"Phase 1: Eliminate transcript replay amplification"}	blake3:DALjfWAYGmItcJxC1_5CsPIwQ-S-vviZp0tolehwiZM
1786289880957016	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzAw		item.create	bn-3rc	{"description":"# Context & Background\nagentbus wait currently uses a byte offset in events.jsonl and --since reads the entire file. Renaming or truncating that file can miss completions, while unbounded scanning causes latency and memory growth.\n\n# Goal\nMove current-or-next completion detection to a compact bounded projection with a monotone generation watermark.\n\n# Approach\nMaintain an atomically rewritten completion index containing a persisted generation and bounded ordered completion records. Capture the generation before session resolution and choose the first qualifying completion. Continue using the snapshot for blocked state.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- wait never returns a completion at or before its entry generation.\n- A completion during session resolution is observed.\n- --since returns the newest qualifying retained result without scanning events.jsonl.\n- Multiple rapid completions remain ordered and the first post-watermark one wins.\n- Retention produces an explicit history-expired result rather than silent fallback.\n\n# Project Value\nMakes verbose log rotation independent from the supervision correctness contract.","kind":"goal","labels":["retention","wait"],"parent":"bn-28h","size":"l","title":"Phase 2: Decouple wait from the verbose event log"}	blake3:k_2QGX2MFybcavPGUPVsMduz9uch07dkk5AyODriUdo
1786289881143412	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzBA		item.create	bn-225	{"description":"# Context & Background\nevents.jsonl is approaching one gigabyte and is appended forever. Once wait no longer depends on byte offsets, this diagnostic history can use ordinary bounded generations.\n\n# Goal\nKeep useful recent replay while enforcing both an age ceiling and a hard byte ceiling.\n\n# Approach\nEnforce one publisher per log path, rotate the active generation before a configured size threshold, retain sealed generations by age, and prune oldest generations until the total cap holds. Preserve events.jsonl as the active path and document tail -F for followers.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Default active generation rotates at 64 MiB.\n- Default history is at most seven days and 512 MiB, apart from one atomic batch overshoot.\n- Two publishers cannot race rotation.\n- Rotation and pruning survive crash and partial artifacts conservatively.\n- The existing legacy log is not deleted before verified cutover.\n\n# Project Value\nPlaces a predictable upper bound on the main source of agentbus disk usage.","kind":"goal","labels":["retention","event-log"],"parent":"bn-28h","size":"l","title":"Phase 3: Rotate and prune verbose event history"}	blake3:kdI_o1icAa1MGc_xUFN1CDWVRvFGOFSGr9F-jjm7kzI
1786289881332875	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzBQ		item.create	bn-372	{"description":"# Context & Background\nregister.jsonl and inbox.jsonl are currently small but append forever. Hooks must never block, and concurrent append makes in-place compaction or rename unsafe without a protocol.\n\n# Goal\nReplace shared append-only hook journals with bounded, race-free ingress while preserving quick best-effort hook behavior.\n\n# Approach\nHave hooks atomically publish uniquely named spool records. Let the observer consume and remove durable records only after folding them. Publish registration state as an observer-owned atomic projection and age out stale spool data under explicit caps. Drain legacy journals during migration.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Hook processes do not wait for observer locks and still exit zero.\n- Concurrent hooks cannot overwrite one another.\n- Observer crash before processing leaves records for recovery.\n- Successfully applied records are deleted.\n- Registration and inbox storage have explicit byte and age caps.\n- Existing hook configurations continue working through migration.\n\n# Project Value\nCompletes bounded ownership for every file agentbus creates, without putting reliability work on agent hot paths.","kind":"goal","labels":["retention","hooks"],"parent":"bn-28h","size":"l","title":"Phase 4: Bound hook ingress and registration state"}	blake3:UKZRaH_xNIziZlKLCXmXGCsq4sha2Rm9xdqURoWwoJs
1786289881524463	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzBg		item.create	bn-36k	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe running publisher writes into the user state directory and serves a Zellij snapshot. The worktree also contains unfinished UI changes that must remain intact. Retention is only complete when the installed service behaves correctly with real agents.\n\n# Goal\nShip the bounded storage design with safe defaults, compatible migration, operational diagnostics, and fresh live evidence.\n\n# Approach\nDocument new files and options, provide conservative migration for legacy JSONL, run focused and full Rust gates, install the binary, restart the publisher deliberately, and smoke-test sessions, wait, and Zellij state before any legacy deletion.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- README and help explain defaults, files, tail behavior, and history expiry.\n- Focused tests, cargo test, fmt check, and clippy with warnings denied pass.\n- Installed service publishes a fresh snapshot and exactly one publisher runs.\n- A live wait returns the correct new answer.\n- Zellij continues showing current agents.\n- Legacy storage removal happens only after validation and is reported.\n\n# Project Value\nTurns code-level retention into a trustworthy always-on operational change.","kind":"goal","labels":["retention","operations"],"parent":"bn-28h","size":"m","title":"Phase 5: Migrate, document, and verify the live service"}	blake3:icgWoPN0YPazdhAHUfZlbxTNgL92_OIv-ffcax4Spyg
1786289969875347	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzBw		item.create	bn-3vz	{"description":"# Context\nThe active recency set is also used as the ownership set for MultiTail and Stream. Leaving that set deletes the cursor and parser state; returning later replays the complete file.\n\n# Implementation\nSeparate polling eligibility from known-stream state. Keep offsets, partial-line bytes, identity suppression, source metadata, and Claude turn state when a file becomes inactive. Prune only files that are definitively removed or superseded.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- A transcript inactive longer than --within resumes at its previous byte.\n- The triggering new line is normalized and published exactly once.\n- Claude result capture survives inactivity mid-turn.\n- Polling remains limited to currently active paths.\n- Memory accounting and stale-entry behavior are documented.","kind":"bug","labels":["transcripts","replay"],"parent":"bn-3mg","size":"m","title":"Retain transcript cursors and parser state across inactivity"}	blake3:oMUjqwIBoynYldqJ57uhodo0RjJywr4j0LAqiNoMytA
1786289970080869	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzCA		item.create	bn-1gc	{"description":"# Context\nIn-memory cursor retention fixes rediscovery during one daemon lifetime but not a restart followed by reactivation of an older transcript.\n\n# Implementation\nAtomically persist a versioned checkpoint projection in the agentbus state directory. Include file identity, byte offset, partial-line handling, and the minimal normalizer state needed for exact continuation. Validate replacement, truncation, malformed state, and checkpoint version conservatively.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Clean restart resumes without republishing committed bytes.\n- A checkpoint never binds to a different inode or replaced file.\n- Truncation and malformed checkpoints cannot fabricate events.\n- Checkpoint writes are atomic and bounded by stale-entry pruning.\n- Startup backfill still reconstructs the active snapshot without publishing history.","kind":"task","labels":["transcripts","recovery"],"parent":"bn-3mg","size":"m","title":"Persist restart-safe transcript checkpoints"}	blake3:MMvXSDACShi_mDqEcviR2ojvody96Cj_r-Ub1TDSN34
1786289970291164	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzCQ		item.create	bn-p7r	{"description":"# Context\nReplay amplification is temporal and can appear correct in snapshots while silently multiplying the event log.\n\n# Implementation\nAdd deterministic temporary-file tests for active to inactive to active transitions, restarts, partial lines, replacement, truncation, and stateful Claude turn completion.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Tests fail against the old drop-and-retrack behavior.\n- Every source publishes each appended fixture event once.\n- Backfilled events affect state but not the output log.\n- Checkpoint corruption and version mismatch fail conservatively.","kind":"task","labels":["tests","transcripts"],"parent":"bn-3mg","size":"s","title":"Add replay and checkpoint regression tests"}	blake3:VENZK3ZW67ztCaIU_K69gFe5kQCqgRP3sNw2Hw2ugC4
1786289970498793	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzCg		item.create	bn-2s6	{"description":"# Context\nCompletion correctness currently depends on offsets into the verbose event log. A separate projection can remain small and stable under log rotation.\n\n# Implementation\nCreate a versioned completion index with a persisted monotone generation and ordered retained turn_end records. Write through a same-directory temporary file and atomic rename. Enforce seven-day, ten-thousand-record, and 64 MiB defaults without splitting a record.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Every published turn_end receives a unique increasing generation.\n- Restart continues above the last durable generation.\n- Readers see either the old or new complete index.\n- Pruning preserves ordering and exposes the earliest retained generation.\n- Oversized individual results have explicit bounded behavior.","kind":"task","labels":["wait","completion"],"parent":"bn-3rc","size":"m","title":"Build a bounded atomic completion index"}	blake3:ePN4LH4qJap_GT8RA9HebV-_rEJ-id8U_DA8C5SHFS8
1786289970706175	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzCw		item.create	bn-2a3	{"description":"# Context\nwait captures a byte offset before session resolution and --since scans all events.jsonl. Both must move together or rotation retains a hidden correctness dependency.\n\n# Implementation\nCapture completion generation before resolving the filter. After resolution, select the earliest matching completion newer than the entry watermark; for --since select the newest retained matching timestamp. Continue checking blocked state through the snapshot and preserve exit codes and output shape.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- A completion during session resolution is returned.\n- A completion at or before entry is never returned without --since.\n- The first of multiple post-entry completions wins.\n- --since does not read events.jsonl.\n- Expired history is distinguishable from no completion and documented.\n- Existing stdout, JSON, blocked, timeout, and error contracts remain compatible.","kind":"task","labels":["wait","query"],"parent":"bn-3rc","size":"m","title":"Move wait and --since onto completion generations"}	blake3:0uftKWw7UIsSQJDdvhT3-QCpG3uyVxnkZtulwcPkphs
1786289970917861	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzDA		item.create	bn-2r4	{"description":"# Context\nThe generation projection replaces the most correctness-sensitive part of agentbus.\n\n# Implementation\nExercise entry races, session discovery, rapid completions, restart generation continuity, atomic replacement, pruning floors, --since boundaries, blocked transitions, and timeout behavior using small deterministic caps.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Tests reproduce the old stale-answer and missed-gap hazards.\n- All watermark ordering cases are deterministic.\n- Retention never silently rewinds or accepts an expired cursor.\n- No test reads a large synthetic verbose log to complete a wait.","kind":"task","labels":["tests","wait"],"parent":"bn-3rc","size":"s","title":"Add completion watermark and retention tests"}	blake3:VGadGbdEtJyDLULboUyW5WSjb8rqOHbyNrQREuOQSZg
1786289971121695	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzDQ		item.create	bn-2a1	{"description":"# Context\nAtomic O_APPEND tolerates accidental multiple observers, but rotation cannot safely support two independent owners.\n\n# Implementation\nAcquire a nonblocking OS lock scoped to the resolved event-log path for publishing watch or scan modes. Keep the descriptor alive for the process lifetime, report the current owner diagnostically where possible, and leave --no-publish readers unaffected.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- A second publisher for the same log exits clearly without writing.\n- A publisher for a different explicit log path remains allowed.\n- Crash and SIGKILL release the kernel lock without stale-file blocking.\n- events --no-publish and query commands require no publisher lock.","kind":"task","labels":["event-log","locking"],"parent":"bn-225","size":"s","title":"Enforce one publisher per event log"}	blake3:XmdDt_48EUt7o7pLXXHBV9yDHgLrnBzM2BZJgph9ckY
1786289971337834	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzDg		item.create	bn-1yt	{"description":"# Context\nWith wait decoupled, events.jsonl is diagnostic replay history and can rotate normally.\n\n# Implementation\nRotate before a batch would cross 64 MiB, naming immutable generations without collision. Prune sealed generations older than seven days and then oldest-first until active plus archives fit 512 MiB. Treat partial or unfamiliar artifacts conservatively and expose CLI overrides.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Active log plus recognized generations stays within the configured hard cap except one atomic batch.\n- Age and byte limits both apply.\n- Rotation never splits or interleaves a JSON line.\n- Current events.jsonl remains the active path.\n- No unrecognized file is deleted.\n- Direct followers are documented to use tail -F.","kind":"task","labels":["event-log","retention"],"parent":"bn-225","size":"m","title":"Implement size and age bounded event generations"}	blake3:VON-HB3IWrEOOeaqA_RHBvw1kbOZnjG751npP1AvJbQ
1786289971543438	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzDw		item.create	bn-1rg	{"description":"# Context\nRetention changes filesystem identity and eventually removes data, so boundary behavior needs more than happy-path unit coverage.\n\n# Implementation\nUse tiny configured sizes and clocks to test batch-boundary rotation, filename collisions, publisher contention, stale lock files, age ordering, hard-cap pruning, crash artifacts, and adoption of the existing unbounded events.jsonl as a legacy generation.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Tests prove no event loss or duplication across rotation.\n- Pruning chooses only sealed recognized generations.\n- An oversized legacy log is preserved until explicit verified cutover.\n- Failures to rotate or prune leave a writable or clearly failed publisher, never silent corruption.","kind":"task","labels":["tests","event-log"],"parent":"bn-225","size":"m","title":"Test rotation, pruning, and legacy cutover"}	blake3:hs2jIqP_aLyB8K0BSad0bN0oSrszGd3L2Ok_VoCNKkA
1786289971756035	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzEA		item.create	bn-1nw	{"description":"# Context\nHooks currently append to shared JSONL. Renaming or compacting that file can race an already-open hook writer, while blocking locks could wedge an agent.\n\n# Implementation\nWrite each hook report to a unique temporary file and atomically rename it into an inbox spool directory. Clamp record size, sanitize names, avoid waiting on daemon-owned locks, and preserve the rule that every hook path exits zero.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Concurrent hook invocations cannot overwrite or interleave records.\n- Observer absence leaves complete records for later processing.\n- Partial temporary files are never treated as ready records.\n- Hook latency remains bounded by one small local write and rename.\n- All error paths remain best effort and exit zero.","kind":"task","labels":["hooks","spool"],"parent":"bn-372","size":"m","title":"Introduce lock-free hook spool publishing"}	blake3:jzohpqMxVmxkcDJmHTOYBEVlX6FS6cBicTjHWoiQxFc
1786289971955843	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzEQ		item.create	bn-cdo	{"description":"# Context\nThe observer must consume durable hook facts exactly enough for state while exposing registration lookup without an append-only journal.\n\n# Implementation\nDrain ready spool files in deterministic order, fold each before removing it, and publish the latest registration map atomically as observer-owned state. Preserve process identity, transcript, mux location, and current inbox precedence rules.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Crash before fold leaves the record; crash after durable fold does not corrupt state.\n- Applied spool files are removed.\n- Query and UI continue resolving pid, transcript, and pane information.\n- Registration publication is a bounded atomic snapshot.\n- A dead registration ages out without requiring hook cooperation.","kind":"task","labels":["hooks","register"],"parent":"bn-372","size":"m","title":"Drain hook spool and publish compact registrations"}	blake3:KNUt4Z3ySmV1EnjBDc0-DHeyVNOnHgpbdXYsl9IwQkQ
1786289972173040	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzEg		item.create	bn-165	{"description":"# Context\nExisting installations already contain register.jsonl and inbox.jsonl, so switching paths without a drain would lose current identities and reports.\n\n# Implementation\nRead legacy journals during a one-way migration, deduplicate latest registration facts, import pending inbox events, mark migration completion atomically, and retain old files until verification. Add age and byte caps for abandoned spool records with visible diagnostics.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Upgrade preserves current live registrations and pending reports.\n- Re-running migration is idempotent.\n- Legacy files are not deleted before verified publication.\n- Spool storage has explicit age and byte ceilings.\n- Tests cover concurrent new spool writes during migration.","kind":"task","labels":["hooks","migration","tests"],"parent":"bn-372","size":"s","title":"Migrate and cap legacy hook journals"}	blake3:SnEWJGYY96k4oA-_3WAK86rFAPSEWKaJThX06qjqZSU
1786289972376863	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzEw		item.create	bn-398	{"description":"# Context\nOperators and scripts currently assume one forever-growing events.jsonl and byte-offset waits.\n\n# Implementation\nUpdate help, README, systemd guidance, and operational commands for checkpoint, completion, generation, lock, and spool files. Explain defaults, overrides, tail -F, history expiry, migration, and how to inspect disk use.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Every new option and state artifact is documented.\n- Default 64 MiB generation, seven-day age, 512 MiB event cap, and completion caps are stated.\n- wait compatibility and history-expired behavior are clear.\n- Recovery and rollback instructions preserve user data.","kind":"task","labels":["docs","operations"],"parent":"bn-36k","size":"s","title":"Document retention files, defaults, and failure modes"}	blake3:xDbs2UQtXQBQ7TD0osZqi5BJVtKMD1-nUQK_QlN_toQ
1786289972584324	codex	itc:v3:AWKcyTkmSTnJOZEAAAAAQbtXVqu6u0AAAAEzFA		item.create	bn-3pa	{"description":"# Context\nThe running process publishes to the Zellij runtime snapshot while this checkout contains pre-existing UI work. Deployment must verify the combined tree and must not silently delete the roughly 895 MB legacy log.\n\n# Implementation\nReview the final diff for ownership, run formatting, all tests, clippy with warnings denied, and focused retention stress tests. Install the binary, restart exactly one publisher, verify fresh snapshot and UI state, perform a real submit plus wait, observe bounded rotation, and only then admit the legacy log to retention.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- Pre-existing UI changes are preserved and tested.\n- cargo fmt check, cargo test, and cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings pass.\n- Exactly one live publisher owns the configured log.\n- Fresh sessions and Zellij state update after restart.\n- A real wait returns the new turn result.\n- Disk-size evidence shows configured bounds.\n- Any material deletion is explicitly reported with recovery status.","kind":"task","labels":["verification","operations"],"parent":"bn-36k","size":"m","title":"Run full gates and perform verified live cutover"}	blake3:Xzr1iQjGmqgIKQCzQSW_4cbj8qRC82w3SbxZItL_Ovo
